Hi Andrea,
Yes, that is easy to do.  See this FAQ:

http://r.iq.harvard.edu/docs/matchit/2.4-20/How_Do_I3.html

Basically you use a command like:


m.out.fr1 <- matchit(treat ~ var1 + var2 + var3, data=dta, distance=dta$pscore)

The formula given at the beginning of the command is just to tell MatchIt the variables on which to calculate balance; it uses the propensity scores in the dta$pscore vector for the matching.

Thanks,
Liz

