You can do the following tweak: create a distance measure so that any given pair in your matched data has the shortest distance.  So for example, if you have 3 pairs, you may assign (0.25, 0.26), (0.5, 0.51), (0.75, 0.76) so that when MatchIt does pairing with nearest neighbor, it returns the same matches.  Then, you can give that distance measure to MatchIt.

Kosuke

